# 🚩 Challenge: [Warmed Up]

## 📝 Challenge Description
![hexdecimal to decimal](../warmedup.png)
Q. What is 0x3D (base 16) in decimal (base 10)?

hints:
1. Submit your answer in our flag format. For example, if your answer was '22', you would submit 'academy{22}' as the flag.

## 🚀  Solution 
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:
1. Python: Open a python terminal and type 0x3D to instantly get 61.
or
2. Linux Terminal / Bash: Run printf '%d\n' 0x3D.
or
3. Web Browser Console: Hit F12, go to the Console tab, and type parseInt("3D", 16).

## 🏁 Flag
academy{61}
